  "id": "representational-change",
  "term": "representational change",
  "definition": "Representational change is a shift in how a person mentally frames a problem, moving beyond the current context and unstated constraints. In psychology, it is used to explain insight problem solving and can also help account for divergent thinking in creativity.",
